r color appears only in these local start pairs.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D15/2/code.py:121:    \"\"\"Return border particles with a unique adjacent arrow marker.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D15/2/code.py:149:    \"\"\"Move particles through same-color corridors; initial direction comes from edge arrows.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D3/0/code.py:166:      - border color appears multiple times\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D10/1/code.py:61:      - border color appears multiple times\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D10/1/code.py:209:      Solving requires aggregating multiple source-center values into that one target region in the same spatial order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D3/1/code.py:643:        tail = list(int_pos)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D3/1/code.py:644:        random.shuffle(tail)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D3/1/code.py:645:        pool.extend(tail)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2d0172a1/D4/2/code.py:40:#     The variant is intentionally narrow: every canonical frame always uses exactly two\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2d0172a1/D4/2/code.py:300:    Key insight: Ignore the hand-drawn contour details; only nesting plus relative side/order matter, and every recovered frame reappears as the same double-border motif.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D13/1/code.py:54:#   starts must remain because the visible change is multiplication, not motion.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D10/2/code.py:157:      - border color appears multiple times\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D10/2/code.py:225:    - Multiple sprites attach to the same grey trail by valid ports; unrelated sprites may also appear elsewhere.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D3/2/code.py:345:      - border color appears multiple times\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/58f5dbd5/D19/0/code.py:92:    Combine multiple color-matched motifs into one carved block pattern and pack the carved blocks.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/58f5dbd5/D19/0/code.py:339:    \"\"\"Return feasible matching-motif multiplicities for the sampled block count.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D15/2/code.py:35:#    - The variant is kept narrow: only the marker identification and flood source\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D15/2/code.py:36:#      multiplicity change. Colors, wall semantics, decoration semantics, and border\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D15/2/code.py:70:#      reuse is unchanged. This keeps the grid legible even when multiple pockets are\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D13/2/code.py:92:# - Multiple particles are assumed not to require collision tie-breaking beyond \"destination cells\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D16/2/code.py:28:#    - Generator forces at least one non-unit slit per instance and prefers multiple speeds in the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D16/2/code.py:37:#      Now an opening can have multiple cells, so we separate:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D16/2/code.py:56:#        narrow slit -> dense beam\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D16/2/code.py:635:    - Every frame has one or two connected openings, and each opening is a 1-3 pixel slit that\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2d0172a1/12/code.py:37:#         2. a large background-only tail remains below and to the right\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/58f5dbd5/D19/1/code.py:213:# Repetition templates: one motif color must fan out to multiple blocks.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D18/0/code.py:73:- Multiple particles in the same grid use the same mechanism, so a human can\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D18/0/code.py:158:    \"\"\"Use a nearby fake-row hint pixel to choose among multiple turn options.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D18/0/code.py:173:    assert len(matched) <= 1, \"multiple matching hints for one blocker\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D7/0/code.py:70:#     gives the human multiple supporting examples of the same mapping behavior.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/58f5dbd5/D19/2/code.py:45:   - The block counts and layouts are unchanged, so the task still includes multiple colors and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D4/0/code.py:125:      - border color appears multiple times\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D6/0/code.py:36:#   cells, so they do not destroy the bar/corridor layout or pile multiple\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D3/0/code.py:57:#     - Multiple beams can share one frame color, but each beam also repeats its own\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b5033c1/18/code.py:82:#    and output padding only appears at row tails.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D7/1/code.py:114:      - border color appears multiple times\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D4/1/code.py:93:      - border color appears multiple times\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b5033c1/25/code.py:48:#    second column uses only three stable code colors. Comparing multiple samples makes it possible\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/58f5dbd5/D2/0/code.py:20:#     was enough to decide the stencil. In this variant, each block color appears on multiple\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/58f5dbd5/D2/0/code.py:108:    - Elsewhere, each block color appears on multiple small motif sprites; one motif shape repeats\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/58f5dbd5/D2/0/code.py:120:    - Color only narrows the candidate pool; the real stencil is the same-colored motif shape that\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D7/3/code.py:114:      - border color appears multiple times\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D7/3/code.py:242:    - Grey cells are split into multiple independent 8-connected path components; each component's two endpoints\n/home/li