nerator requires multiple trimmed sides and a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/31/code.py:49:#   belong to the same object and must not create multiple overlapping patches.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b5033c1/1/code.py:35:#    - Snake length is chosen as a multiple of K, with 4..7 rows after folding, so\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b5033c1/1/code.py:79:#    - The palette size is capped at 3..5 and every chosen color appears multiple times\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b5033c1/1/code.py:90:#      Guarantee: generator chooses target lengths from multiples of K only.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D10/1/code.py:77:# - Because accepted samples must show multiple shells, a human sees outward\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D10/1/code.py:115:        assert total <= 1, \"ambiguous turn: multiple perpendicular mouths\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b5033c1/3/code.py:249:            tail = dfs(remaining - value, parts_left - 1)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b5033c1/3/code.py:250:            if tail is not None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b5033c1/3/code.py:251:                return [value, *tail]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/27/code.py:32:#    1/2/3, so the output shows multiple 3x3/5x5/7x7 patches rather than a single\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:3:# Change: 无符号编码（颜色匹配规则由示例隐含给出）... → 精灵内部的方向箭头标记\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:13:     an explicit 3-pixel arrow inside each source sprite.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:15:     Sources replace the single interior pixel with a 3-pixel arrowhead made from the transfer color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:18:       new: source.arrow points right, exactly one destination lies to the right of that source ->\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:19:            copy source.arrow color into that destination center\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:20:     The path still tells us which two sprites are destinations; the arrow only decides source->target.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:23:   - The arrow alphabet is limited to four global directions: up/down/left/right.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:24:   - Each sample contains exactly two arrow-bearing sources so the symbol is repeated and decodable.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:33:     The arrow therefore uses only the center and corners, leaving cardinal border cells untouched.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:37:   - Arrow sources must be fully visible so their 3-pixel symbols are never clipped or ambiguous.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:43:     by the grey path, while the deleted source sprites visibly contain arrowheads that point toward\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:46:     solver to use the arrows.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:49:   - Only box sprites are used in this variant. That keeps the arrow symbols readable and avoids\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:51:   - Arrows are 3-pixel corner-and-center motifs (`^`, `v`, `<`, `>`) inside a 3x3 frame, which is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:55:   - The color transferred to a destination is simply the arrow color shown inside the matching source.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:59:   - Assumption: every arrow source is a full 3x3 box with one of four known 3-pixel patterns.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:136:    Source sprites have a 3-pixel inner arrow pattern.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:192:def _decode_arrow(sprite: dict) -> str | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/