ils(grid: np.ndarray) -> tuple[np.ndarray, dict]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D10/3/code.py:241:    - Structural walls split the background into multiple enclosed chambers that\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D10/3/code.py:256:    out, _meta = _solve_details(grid)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D10/3/code.py:353:    out, meta = _solve_details(inp)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D10/2/code.py:143:    \"\"\"Move each magenta particle along aligned narrow corridors.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b5033c1/11/code.py:58:#    band lengths reappear in multiple colors, so choosing the wrong endpoint visibly changes the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2d0172a1/D11/2/code.py:35:#       difficulty is \"multiple independent hierarchies\" rather than unrelated noise.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D12/2/code.py:24:#    continuation is only the completed tail of the segment that was clipped by\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D12/2/code.py:35:#    still need multiple objects, multiple gap patterns, and repeated beam\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D12/2/code.py:50:#      start so it can mirror the clipped tail correctly.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D12/2/code.py:314:            assert not in_bounds(nxt), \"completed tail should stay outside the original crop\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D12/2/code.py:617:    Emit colored beams from framed 2x2 blocks, then enlarge the canvas to reveal clipped tails.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6ffbe589/D2/2/code.py:64:#   one another, and there is no stacking of multiple markers in one local region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D13/0/code.py:55:#     - the variant differs from the original on multiple border pixels, not just one center\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D13/0/code.py:113:      - border color appears multiple times\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D2