/code.py:73:# - Each sample contains multiple active repairs and multiple inactive black\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D7/0/code.py:52:#    - Assumption: multiple bursts can overlap safely. Generator guarantee: all bursts use\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/221dfab4/D4/1/code.py:23:#   look identical to the old one. The generator therefore forces multiple witness blobs\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b5033c1/16/code.py:168:                raise ValueError(\"found multiple legend-like components\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b5033c1/16/code.py:172:                raise ValueError(\"found multiple non-legend components\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D13/2/code.py:156:      - border color appears multiple times\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7491f3cf/D9/0/code.py:240:            assert indicator is None, \"multiple 8-isolated cue pixels\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/37/code.py:37:#    - Both regions still carry multiple dents. Each sample therefore shows\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/58f5dbd5/D16/1/code.py:63:# - The legend uses only a narrow 2-column corner strip with blank rows between pairs, so it is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b5033c1/10/code.py:173:            raise ValueError(\"non-hub branch node has multiple forward neighbors\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7491f3cf/D2/0/code.py:165:            assert indicator is None, \"multiple 8-isolated cue pixels\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/8/code.py:116:            assert marker is None, \"multiple corner singleton markers found\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D6/0/code.py:110:      - border color appears multiple times\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D4/2/code.py:54:#     - gap count is limited to 1..3 to avoid dense clutter once multiple differently sized framed blocks coexist\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/29/code.py:18:#      rectangle. D13 moves the alignment rule from \"match the arm tip\" to \"center on\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/29/code.py:51:#      their width/height clearly matches the whole plus bbox rather than just the arm tip.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/29/code.py:190:      narrow arm tip. One marker ray may already be fully pre-expanded as an example.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7491f3cf/D7/2/code.py:159:                assert t1_color not in markers, \"multiple tile1-colored markers in cue tile\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7491f3cf/D7/2/code.py:162:                assert t2_color not in markers, \"multiple tile2-colored markers in cue tile\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/221dfab4/D13/0/code.py:33:#    close to the original. The generator therefore forces multiple blocked tracks at\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7491f3cf/D2/1/code.py:44:#        sparse: 6-8 pixels, dense: 11-13 pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7491f3cf/D2/1/code.py:283:            assert indicator is None, \"multiple 8-isolated cue pixels\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b5033c1/21/code.py:77:#    legend. The generator uses every source color multiple times along the snake and chooses target\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b5033c1/21/code.py:178:                raise ValueError(\"found multiple legend-like components\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b5033c1/21/code.py:182:                raise ValueError(\"found multiple non-legend components\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D6/1/code.py:42:#      border remains with an empty middle. Since every sample has multiple such sprites, the rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D6/1/code.py:113:      - border color appears multiple times\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6ffbe589/D1/3/code.py:35:#     - a 3-pixel cue centered near row 5.0 but with unrelated color 9\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/42/code.py:24:#   enough that merge-vs-naive stamping changes multiple cells and is easy to see.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/3/code.py:259:    - Border-touching wall pieces come in multiple structural colors (blue and red), while interior\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b5033c1/19/code.py:25:#    multiple regions, often including at least one lexicographically earlier cell\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/221dfab4/D13/1/code.py:35:#    a large blob. The traced stride sequence must deviate from the original fixed stride on multiple\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7491f3cf/D8/1/code.py:349:            assert indicator is None, \"multiple 8-isolated cue pixels\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/11/code.py:45:#     one large border plus multiple detached small rings, making D20/0 easy to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/11/code.py:65:#   - Multiple visible decorations are greedily spaced so their halos are also\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/35/code.py:47:#    - Each sample visibly contains teal-marked black bites in background plus multiple black\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D6/3/code.py:107:      - border color appears multiple times\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/25/code.py:27:#    rule is repeated multiple times in each sample. Rays still use the original\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/58f5dbd5/D3/0/code.py:36:#    - Decoration cells vary per motif (1-3 pixels), so the output is visibly different from the original carve-only\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/7/code.py:79:#     - The generator requires each visible role to contain multiple cells, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/7/code.py:80:#       the dashed ring to omit multiple alternating candidates, so the rule is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D6/2/code.py:17:#   at its center remains as one isolated color-3 pixel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D6/2/code.py:107:      - border color appears multiple times\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/26/code.py:24:#    - Direction still has only four cardinal values and repeats across multiple objects.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/17/code.py:99:#     colors, plus at least one 9x9 case. That gives the human solver multiple\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b5033c1/28/code.py:23:#    The generator uses 3-5 colors and chooses total path length as an exact multiple of that\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b5033c1/28/code.py:56:#      Guaranteed by using every palette color and choosing total length as a multiple of it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7b5033c1/D1/0/code.py:20:#    multiple of K with at least 4 rows. This avoids visually weak cases such as a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7b5033c1/D1/0/code.py:45:#      generator choosing `target_len` from multiples of K only.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7491f3cf/D16/0/code.py:64:#    - With 2-4 examples where the cue appears in multiple positions, the new rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/2/code.py:47:#     the solver must now parse multiple starts, keep per-source reach logic, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/2/code.py:62:#   - The original wall test used one reach0. With multiple sources that would miss\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/2/code.py:307:    chamber can be reachable from multiple markers, so the final boundary is a distance-based\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b5033c1/13/code.py:67:#   or extra decorations. The output is a small compact rectangle with only tail\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D14/0/code.py:108:      - border color appears multiple times\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/38/code.py:383:      patch shape, and extra teal away from the black holes marks where multiple dent\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cbebaa4b/D2/1/code.py:49:      examples of pieces with multiple red sides; on those pieces the green side\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/16/code.py:26:#          carve long narrow chambers rather than roughly square rooms.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b5033c1/23/code.py:30:#    - K is restricted to 3..5, and path length is chosen from multiples of K with\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b5033c1/23/code.py:86:#      by choosing target lengths from multiples of `color_count`.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D14/1/code.py:147:      - border color appears multiple times\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/221dfab4/D14/2/code.py:11:#    Variant: the seed is an L-shaped yellow border component in one corner, e.g.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7491f3cf/D3/0/code.py:299:            assert indicator is None, \"multiple 8-isolated cue pixels\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:3:# Name: 箭头精灵大瓦片颜色循环\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:18:#    - Anchor cue: the big monochrome objects are now rotated arrow sprites.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:25:#    Example: if a right-pointing arrow carries a 3x2 seed on its lower flank,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:30:#    The variant would become ambiguous if arrow directions, seed sizes, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:33:#    - one arrow template family,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:37:#    Seeds still differ by internal texture and arrow orientation, so the combo\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:42:#      clockwise flank, orthogonal to the ray. We must recognize arrow shape.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:45:#      origin from the matched arrow geometry plus a globally inferred tile size.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:50:#      color by exact arrow-shape matches.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:53:#    The generator is output-first. It places arrows with one-cell guard bands,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:55:#    any previous non-background payload. This guarantees that each arrow has\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:56:#    exactly one adjacent non-arrow component and label-based extraction stays\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:61:#    shows all three cues: the arrow points one way while the seed sits on a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:63:#    the same geometry but cycle their colors. Other arrows reuse the same size\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:68:#    other, and each grid uses only 2-4 arrows. This prevents component merges\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:74:#    permutation multiple times; the solver never has to guess an unseen mapping.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:79:#    - every sample uses at least two arrow orientations,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:85:#    - All arrows share one of the known templates, up to rotation.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:87:#    - Exactly one adjacent marker component per arrow is present.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:196:def _oriented_arrow_spec(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:206:def _match_arrow_component(mask: np.ndarray) -> dict | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:210:            rotated, launch_local, attach_normal = _oriented_arrow_spec(spec, direction_name)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:221:def _detect_arrow_color(grid: np.ndarray, *, bg: int) -> int | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:235:            if _match_arrow_component(local) is None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:399:    Extend large marker tiles from arrow anchors, cycling colors on every repeated chunk.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:403:    - One non-background color forms several rotated arrow sprites from a small fixed template family.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:404:    - Each arrow has exactly one adjacent large rectangular seed marker on a side flank, and exactly one arrow in the grid keeps its full long ray as the clue.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:407:    - Read each arrow's pointing direction from its silhouette rather than from the marker attachment side.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:408:    - Infer the shared seed-tile size from the compact markers, reconstruct the clue arrow's first tile, and learn a global color permutation by comparing consecutive full chunks on the long clue ray.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:409:    - For every arrow, repeat its seed rectangle outward in the arrow direction until the boundary, applying one more step of the learned color cycle after each whole-tile advance; arrow pixels are never overwritten.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:412:    The task now fuses three cues: arrow shape gives direction, the payload is a large textured rectangle, and the single long example ray reveals that repetition preserves geometry but rotates colors through a fixed global cycle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:419:    arrow_color = _detect_arrow_color(g, bg=int(bg))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:420:    if arrow_color is None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:423:    arrow_lab, an = label_mask(g == int(arrow_color), connectivity=4)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:424:    non_mask = (g != int(bg)) & (g != int(arrow_color))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:428:    arrow_records: list[dict] = []\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:431:        arrow_mask = arrow_lab == int(ak)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:432:        arrow_coords = np.argwhere(arrow_mask)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:433:        if arrow_coords.size == 0:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:436:        ar0, ac0, ar1, ac1 = bbox_coords(arrow_coords)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:437:        local_arrow = g[int(ar0) : int(ar1) + 1, int(ac0) : int(ac1) + 1] == int(arrow_color)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:438:        matched = _match_arrow_component(local_arrow)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:443:        for r, c in arrow_coords:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:467:        arrow_records.append(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:475:    if not arrow_records:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:484:    for record in arrow_records:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:501:        if np.any(tile == int(bg)) or np.any(tile == int(arrow_color)):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:527:            protect={int(arrow_color)},\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:680:def _place_arrow_and_ray(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:691:    arrow_guard: np.ndarray,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:694:    arrow_color: int,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:699:    patch, launch_local, attach_normal = _oriented_arrow_spec(spec, direction_name)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:711:        arr