colors[2:]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D5/2/code.py:556:    random.shuffle(tail)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D5/2/code.py:557:    marker_colors = marker_colors[:2] + tail\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/5/code.py:40:#      colors. This gives multiple endpoint lengths without introducing a large\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/31/code.py:16:#   output transform; it is a deliberately narrower, cleaner input family.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/31/code.py:25:#   distractors of other colors, but not on multiple same-colored candidates. In this combo, a stricter\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D4/1/code.py:84:    \"\"\"Rows/cols at multiples of 3 inside the centered 6x6 stamp box.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/4/code.py:213:            assert indicator is None, \"multiple 8-isolated cue pixels\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8698868d/D4/3/code.py:85:#    - Fill colors are pairwise distinct, which gives multiple independent examples\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/27/code.py:51:#       accumulates holes from multiple motifs instead of one.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/27/code.py:243:    - The preset block holes are not output noise; they are the matching key that identifies which disconnected motif sequence belongs to that block, while repeated same-layout motifs mean carving must be accumulated over multiple rounds.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/78332cb0/D4/0/code.py:219:    assert len(chain_h) <= 1 and len(chain_v) <= 1, \"ambiguous: multiple chains found\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/34/code.py:44:#      tail contains bg holes. Color-map inference therefore ignores positions\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/34/code.py:65:#    Reserving whole chunk corridors prevents overlapping partial tails.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/34/code.py:264:d