ple adjacent marker components.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/13/code.py:79:# - Because seeds remain small and aligned to arm tips, the solver can infer the same\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/13/code.py:635:    \"\"\"Erase every ray tail so the input keeps only compact seeds on every arm.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/23/code.py:526:            assert indicator is None, \"multiple 8-isolated cue pixels\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b7bacbf/1/code.py:30:#      shell often breaks into multiple pieces, so it cannot be reused directly. The combo instead uses the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D4/3/code.py:177:                    f\"Line {li} ({'row' if by_row else 'col'}) has multiple aligned companions: {runs}\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D9/3/code.py:19:#    - Variant sprite logic here: each component has one \"tip\" cell with exactly three\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D9/3/code.py:20:#      4-neighbors outside the component; that tip color matches a border anchor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D9/3/code.py:27:#      its 4-neighbors are background / outside the component; the exposed tip has score 3,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D9/3/code.py:28:#      every other sprite cell has score <= 2, so the anchor-color tip is selected.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D9/3/code.py:30:#    - The change is visually observable because the anchor color appears multiple times\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D9/3/code.py:31:#      inside the sprite, but only one occurrence sits on a protruding tip.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D9/3/code.py:47:#    - Every generated tip is fully inside the grid before motion, so its 4-neighbor exposure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D9/3/code.py:59:#    - Sprites use a thick base body plus one protruding tip, which is visually easy to parse.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D9/3/code.py:69:    Slide interior sprites so their most exposed tip-pixel lands on the matching border anchor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D9/3/code.py:273:def _tip_candidates(body):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D9/3/code.py:303:        tip_options = _tip_candidates(raw_body)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D9/3/code.py:304:        if not tip_options:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D9/3/code.py:306:        tip, attach = random.choice(tip_options)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D9/3/code.py:307:        raw_comp = set(raw_body) | {tip}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D9/3/code.py:310:        tip = (tip[0] - r0, tip[1] - c0)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D9/3/code.py:312:        comp = set(body) | {tip}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D9/3/code.py:314:        if _cell_exposure(comp, tip) != 3:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D9/3/code.py:348:        for r, c in marker_body_cells | {tip}:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D9/3/code.py:354:            \"offset\": (tip[0] - r0, tip[1] - c0),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/23/code.py:47:#      checks every painted cell for overlap, then derives the input by erasing every ray tail.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/23/code.py:57:#    - Rays are generated disjointly in the full scene, and inputs erase all tails, so the visible\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/23/code.py:68:#      tails. If any of these control variables drift back to the base task, the combo degenerates.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/23/code.py:74:#      attempt that would create overlap, ambiguous attachment, or too-short diagonal tails.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/23/code.py:502:    \"\"\"Erase every diagonal tail so only compact corner seeds remain in the input.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8698868d/D15/2/code.py:111:    - Unlike the base task, the same sprite may serve multiple frames if that hole count\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8698868d/D15/2/code.py:112:      appears multiple times among the frames.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/22/code.py:191:                assert quadrant not in markers, \"multiple markers for one quadrant\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cbebaa4b/D11/2/code.py:28:#      L-shaped arrangement. It still contains red, but every attempted red-on-red translation\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b7bacbf/3/code.py:11:#       1. exactly one border seed now launches multiple active lines\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b7bacbf/3/code.py:30:#       - one seed now causes multiple fill colors\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b7bacbf/3/code.py:31:#       - one line color now fills multiple separated cavities because its line has true branches\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b7bacbf/3/code.py:38:#       multiple distant cavities\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b7bacbf/3/code.py:48:#         broken, because the single seed now fans out into multiple colored trees\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b7bacbf/3/code.py:61:#     - leaf loops are anchored near segment tails so the \"branch end -> frame ring\" relation is visible\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b7bacbf/3/code.py:168:    One border seed fans out into multiple branching line trees, and every cavity touching one\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b7bacbf/3/code.py:174:    - The seed 4-touches multiple different line colors; each line color forms its own 8-connected\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b7bacbf/3/code.py:441:def _extend_tip_path_inplace(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b7bacbf/3/code.py:445:    tip: tuple[int, int],\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b7bacbf/3/code.py:453:    cur = tip\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b7bacbf/3/code.py