e contains multiple companion-pair lines and at least\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D15/1/code.py:191:            f\"Line {li} ({'row' if by_row else 'col'}) has multiple aligned \"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/eee78d87/D13/1/code.py:37:#   - The freedom stays controlled: no extra colors, no rotations, no multiple recursive\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/11/code.py:120:      same-colored motif shape appears multiple times while a different same-colored motif is present as a decoy.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/30/code.py:48:#   the canonical seed strip can still be read directly from the arm tip it touches.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/30/code.py:299:    - Every plus has exactly one canonical seed strip touching one arm tip; some inputs keep the true\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/12/code.py:34:#   fusion evidence (multiple mixed-color overlap cells, spanning more than one\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/12/code.py:159:            assert indicator is None, \"multiple 8-isolated cue pixels\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D2/0/code.py:100:        # If marker appears multiple times, prefer one attached to the main body (4-adjacent to non-marker).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8698868d/D18/2/code.py:34:#    - The inward corridor is narrow (width 1, depth 1-2) so the frame remains easy to recognize\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D13/2/code.py:197:                    f\"Line {li} ({'row' if by_row else 'col'}) has multiple aligned \"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D13/2/code.py:201:                    f\"Line {li} ({'row' if by_row else 'col'}) has multiple companion colors\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/7/code.py:59:#    - The legend is confined to a narrow corner strip with blank separator rows.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/14/code.py:40:#    commit. Seed tiles remain edge-adjacent to exactly one arm tip and must match that arm tip's\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/14/code.py:41:#    cross-axis span. The 5x4 diamond template only allows vertical rays because its lateral tips\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/14/code.py:51:#    therefore visually reserved for anchors, while marker/ray material stays narrow and readable.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/14/code.py:64:#    seeds match the touched arm-tip span. generate_input() constructs only inputs meeting those\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/14/code.py:215:    - Infer the attachment side locally for that anchor, require the seed span to match that anchor's own arm-tip span, and repeat the seed tile away from the anchor to the boundary.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/1/code.py:207:    Move a compact water plug through a wall-bounded corridor until the corridor ends or narrows.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/1/code.py:212:    - The source plug starts at one endpoint of the reachable corridor. Downstream sections may bend and may later narrow.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/1/code.py:218:    - Relocate the plug to the last reachable placement before the corridor terminates or becomes too narrow.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/1/code.py:377:            \"blocked_tail\": int(len(path) - len(reachable)),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D2/3/code.py:29:#   color for multiple sprites would force them to stack, so the generator now uses one sprite\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e87109e9/D9/1/code.py:39:#      otherwise widened or narrowed segments would be lost.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e87109e9/D9/1/code.py:259:      whether the next segment becomes narrower or wider.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D6/3/code.py:163:            f\"Line {li} ({'row' if by_row else 'col'}) has multiple aligned companions: {aligned_hits}\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8b7bacbf/D9/3/code.py:31:#       still includes: 1-2 seeds, multiple attached frames, optional distractors,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/12/code.py:11:#      collapsed so every plus keeps only its compact seed and no ray tail at all.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/12/code.py:38:#      arm-tip span. The generator keeps that invariant to avoid ambiguous phase shifts.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/12/code.py:500:    \"\"\"Prefer underused directions so one sample usually exhibits multiple branches.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/12/code.py:513:    With no pre-expanded clue, multiple attachment directions in one example make the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/12/code.py:537:    \"\"\"Erase every ray tail so the input keeps only compact seeds and visible source pluses.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b7bacbf/2/code.py:22:#    - Keep 1-2 seeds, repeated frame colors, multiple frames, and optional distractors so the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b7bacbf/2/code.py:26:#      keeps the visual degree of freedom narrow and repeatable across 2-4 ARC examples.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/32/code.py:64:#       There is no stacking of multiple symbol systems onto the same cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e87109e9/D19/1/code.py:199:    assert len(hits) == 1, \"beam footprint must not hit multiple obstacles at once\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/18/code.py:28:#      fused: hollow cross/L already exposes multiple branch-tip red pairs -> the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/18/code.py:29:#      first children must land on those tip ends -> later growth still proceeds\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/18/code.py:34:#      with fixed masks and fixed tip-side counts. This keeps recognition human-\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/18/code.py:36:#    - Cross anchors always use 3 direct tip ports; L anchors always use 2. That\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/18/code.py:37:#      forces multiple branch ends to matter without introducing too many degrees\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/18/code.py:47:#      non-convex anchors, so anchor masks now carry explicit tip-side geometry\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/18/code.py:60:#      a plain block, but a hollow thick cross or hollow thick L with tip reds.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/18/code.py:70:#      geometric: recognize a hollow cross/L anchor and use its branch-tip reds as\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/18/code.py:223:    - Red (2) connector pixels lie on sprite boundaries; on the anchor they sit at branch tips rather than on a plain rectangular face.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/18/code.py:231:    - The reconstruction is still governed by red-pixel pairing, but the initial docking targets now come from the tip ends of a hollow non-convex anchor, so the solver must recognize anchor geometry by shape instead of by a solid yellow block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/2/code.py:16:#    \"air\" is no longer the transport medium. Instead, color 8 marks a narrow pipe network.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D14/0/code.py:96:    - A shooting-direction line may contain multiple repeated colors.  Each such\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D14/0/code.py:120:    recovered multiple times on the same row/column.  The important separation is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/17/code.py:55:#    - The rule is recoverable from 2-4 examples because the generator repeats the size relation multiple\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D9/0/code.py:36:#    keeps 2-4 assemblies and usually multiple movers so the crop is visible without\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D9/0/code.py:58:#    input, usually with margins on multiple sides. Across examples a human can see\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/29/code.py:33:#      3-pixel templates. This keeps the spatial hypothesis learnable instead of exploding into\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/29/code.py:46:#    - Pattern matching becomes ambiguous if a target color appears multiple times. The new solver\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e87109e9/D2/1/code.py:49:#    old clockwise interpretation on the exact same input by multiple pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D10/2/code.py:41:#     visible_difference: a single line now contains multiple colored beat segments instead of one global fill\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D10/2/code.py:43:#     - multiple companions are allowed but capped at 3 so the rule stays visible in 2-4 examples\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D10/2/code.py:145:            f\"Line {li} ({'row' if by_row else 'col'}) has multiple repeating colors: \"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8b7bacbf/D2/1/code.py:26:#         - multiple leaves extend into different interior regions\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8b7bacbf/D2/1/code.py:27:#         - loops can be attached on different branches, so multiple separated cavities fill\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8b7bacbf/D2/1/code.py:91:#     - loops are attached to multiple different limbs, so the output shows several separated\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8b7bacbf/D2/1/code.py:447:def _extend_tip_path_inplace(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8b7bacbf/D2/1/code.py:451:    tip: tuple[int, int],\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8b7bacbf/D2/1/code.py:457:    cur = tip\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8b7bacbf/D2/1/code.py:459:    dr_bias, dc_bias = _bias_for(tip, h, w, rng)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8b7bacbf/D2/1/code.py:527:                _extend_tip_path_inplace(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8b7bacbf/D2/1/code.py:563:    