).\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8b7bacbf/D3/1/code.py:582:    # than 2 cells to expose multiple alternations rather than a trivial swap.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/33/code.py:26:      step 1 can only use A, because the anchor exposes a red tail and A is the only piece whose\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/33/code.py:28:      after A attaches, the only live tail is A's blue pair, so B-like middle pieces become eligible.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/33/code.py:47:      tracks one active tail group plus its color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/33/code.py:70:    - If a piece is not terminal, its unmarked outgoing pair is the unique next chain tail after placement.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/33/code.py:238:    - The active chain tail determines both legality conditions: the incoming side must overlap\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/33/code.py:239:      the current tail coordinates exactly, and its connector color must match the current tail color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/33/code.py:240:      After attachment, the piece's other connector pair becomes the new tail; terminal pieces have no outgoing pair.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/33/code.py:243:    connector color says at which stage that side becomes legal, and the chain topology says there is only one live tail to match.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/33/code.py:283:    active_tail = _abs_group(anchor_side[\"cells\"], ar0, ac0)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/33/code.py:291:        tail: tuple[tuple[int, int], ...] | None,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/33/code.py:292:        tail_color: int | None,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/33/code.py:298:            if tail is None and len(pc) == target_unique_ports and all(v == 2 for v in pc.values()):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new