ome/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/9/code.py:42:#    - Each sample shows repeated evidence for both changes: multiple joins eliminate\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c7f57c3e/D1/0/code.py:35:#       shape cue remains visible at multiple scales.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8e5c0c38/D2/3/code.py:50:    - Objects remain in separated regions, so no area contains multiple unrelated structures layered together.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c7f57c3e/D1/1/code.py:35:#     not_too_simple: \"each size group appears multiple times, preventing a lone outlier from making the rule ambiguous\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c7f57c3e/D1/1/code.py:49:#       - \"large bbox dimensions are integer multiples of small bbox dimensions\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c7f57c3e/D1/1/code.py:131:    assert len(comps) >= 4, \"grid must contain multiple sprites from both size groups\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/7/code.py:41:#      inferred rule from multiple examples.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/7/code.py:68:#      is therefore a strong, visible consequence rather than a subtle detail.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8e5c0c38/17/code.py:34:   - Marker geometry is also narrow: a short 1xk or kx1 segment outside the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/28/code.py:31:     1. The legend is still a compact square with an L-shaped border, but it is pasted on\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/28/code.py:96:   - The generator uses all four edges, multiple border colors, and all four interior sizes\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/21/code.py:24:#      Blue and green always repeat, so the batch rule is visually supported by multiple\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D15/2/code.py:25:#    - Keep 1-3 anchor colors and 3-5 sprites so multiple components still reuse the same anchor color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D20/0/code.py:28:#    - The change is intentionally narrow: only D20 changes. Water motion,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D20/0/code.py:34:#    - Samples are rejected unless the output contains multiple wet pixels. This\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d59b0160/34/code.py:56:#    - `main()` assumes the smallest top-left L-shaped border is the legend. The generator\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/4/code.py:210:    tail = _translated_port(anchor[\"ports\"][0], ar0, ac0)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/4/code.py:211:    occupied_reds = set(tail)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/4/code.py:217:        active_tail: frozenset[tuple[int, int]] | None,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/4/code.py:224:            if active_tail is None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/4/code.py:227:        if active_tail is None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/4/code.py:235:                pos = _align_port(active_tail, port[\"cells\"])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/4/code.py:246:                    if moved == active_tail:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/4/code.py:277:            next_tail = None\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/4/code.py:282:                    next_tail = moved\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/4/code.py:285:            if next_remaining and next_tail is None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/4/code.py:287:            if not next_remaining and next_tail is not None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/4/code.py:293:                next_tail,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/4/code.py:300:    dfs(placed, rest, tail, occupied_reds, \"main\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/4/code.py:315:    - The first attached sprite must be a main sprite; after that, each next sprite must attach only to the current chain tail and must switch role relative to the previous sprite.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/4/code.py:316:    - Keep relaying the tail forward until all sprites are consumed and the last sprite closes the chain with no unused port left.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/4/code.py:319:    - Red ports still determine geometric alignment, but they are no longer sufficient by themselves: the solver must track both the unique active tail and the required next role in the main/aux alternation.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/20/code.py:17:#      touching the blue tail. If the red anchor sits on the top edge at column 8, the combo\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/20/code.py:20:#      or align a blue tail cell, producing a different motion.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/20/code.py:24:#    - Anchors remain 1-3 colors and sprites remain 3-5, so anchor colors repeat across multiple\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/20/code.py:26:#    - When multiple anchors exist, minority colors are often chosen from a different anchor color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/20/code.py:35:#      the minority patch. The generator enforces this by attaching the tail through one connector.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/20/code.py:44:#    - The minority tail is forced to start in a direction that changes the relevant alignment\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/20/code.py:45:#      coordinate, guaranteeing that \"align majority connector\" and \"align minority tail\" differ.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/20/code.py:48:#      The small odd-colored tail often reuses another anchor color, so a human can see that the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/20/code.py:318:    - Interior sprites are isolated two-color components with a large dominant region and a small attached minority tail.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/20/code.py:323:    - Within that majority region, use the unique majority-colored cell touching the minority tail as the alignment point.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/20/code.py:327:    - The conspicuous large color now controls both which anchor a sprite follows and which internal point is aligned, so the small odd-colored tail is a decoy rather than the key.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/20/code.py:513:def _tail_start_candidates(marker_cells, connector, motion_axis):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/20/code.py:531:def _tail_frontier(tail, marker_cells):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/20/code.py:533:    for r, c in tail:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/20/code.py:536:            if cell in tail or cell in marker_cells:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/20/code.py:544:def _grow_tail(marker_cells, connector, area, motion_axis):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/20/code.py:545:    for start in _tail_start_candidates(marker_cells, connector, motion_axis):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/20/code.py:546:        tail = {start}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/20/code.py:547:        while len(tail) < area:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/20/code.py:548:            frontier = _tail_frontier(tail, marker_cells)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/20/code.py:551:            tail.add(random.choice(frontier))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/20/code.py:552:        if len(tail) == area:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/20/code.py:553:            return tail\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/20/code.py:563:            tail = _grow_tail(marker_cells, connector, body_area, motion_axis)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/20/code.py:564:            if tail is None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/20/code.py:566:            all_cells = set(marker_cells) | set(tail)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/20/code.py:571:            for r, c in tail:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D20/1/code.py:18:#      original: water spills from the right source into the narrow central basin; the untouched left\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D20/1/code.py:48:#      which keeps the scene readable instead of erasing multiple unrelated layers at once.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c7f57c3e/D4/0/code.py:47:#   - multiple sprites at mixed scales\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D6/1/code.py:56:#    - Samples still mix multiple sprites and repeated marker colors, so the solver must infer the axis\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/9/code.py:14:#     - After solving on the full canvas, the output is cropped to the narrow strip containing the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/9/code.py:28:#     - Every anchor gets exactly one sprite. Reusing a center color for multiple sprites would force\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/9/code.py:29:#       multiple bodies to collide on the same target cell, so the generator forbids that.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/9/code.py:128:    - After reconstructing the full solved canvas, keep only the narrow strip that contains the crosshairs and solved sprites.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8e5c0c38/21/code.py:170:                raise ValueError(f\"multiple legend components for color {color}\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/10/code.py:104:    out, _details = _solve_variant(grid, return_details=True)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/10/code.py:108:def _solve_variant(grid: np.ndarray, *, return_details: bool = False) -> tuple[np.ndarray, dict] | np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/10/code.py:226:    details = {\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/10/code.py:235:    if not return_d