e cross-axis span of the arm tip that launches the marker.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/20/code.py:38:#    the minimal rectangle containing that container, those 3 pixels, and the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/1/code.py:18:#      so its L shape exactly overlays that station's visible orientation.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/1/code.py:49:#   3. The grid avoids stacking multiple cue systems on the same cells: labels do matching, the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7c66cb00/2/code.py:59:    - B pieces are narrow rectangles placed far enough from the notch columns to avoid overlap inside bars\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D2/1/code.py:10:      - two 3-pixel L-corners on one bbox diagonal, or\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D2/1/code.py:25:      - expected L-shaped anchors at bbox corners\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D2/1/code.py:90:      This is structurally signposted in the input, so even when multiple colors appear, the mapping is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/2/code.py:15:#      2) Multiple movers are no longer independent. We first compute every\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b3084d4/5/code.py:9:#   Fused: the anchor carries a 2- or 3-pixel grey line at its corner. After rotating\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7c66cb00/16/code.py:35:#    2-3 sprites are sampled so multiple examples support \"inner color chooses\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d59b0160/D17/1/code.py:45:#    - Samples always contain multiple matching components, and at least one smaller matching component survives.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/0/code.py:23:#     - old flow: detect plus component -> find adjacent seed -> use arm-tip span as nozzle\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/0/code.py:37:#     - the old arm-tip alignment asserts are invalid because frames have no arm nozzles;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/0/code.py:41:#     - different objects must neither overlap nor 4-touch each other, otherwise multiple\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/bf45cf4b/D8/2/code.py:105:        # Prefer the strongest base-task signatures if multiple colors somehow pass:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/11/code.py:67:   - Exactly one station group has multiple 4-connected lobes, and every train docks\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/7/code.py:17:#    head turns into an 8-colored tip and the former bulk turns into 5.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/7/code.py:677:    tip_r, tip_c = HEAD_TIPS[direction]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/7/code.py:682:        target_tip = (r0 - gap, random.randint(c0, c1) + jitter)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/7/code.py:684:        target_tip = (r1 + gap, random.randint(c0, c1) + jitter)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/7/code.py:686:        target_tip = (random.randint(r0, r1) + jitter, c0 - gap)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/7/code.py:688:        target_tip = (random.randint(r0, r1) + jitter, c1 + gap)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/7/code.py:689:    dr = target_tip[0] - tip_r\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/7/code.py:690:    dc = target_tip[1] - tip_c\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:3:# Change: '+'精灵为小型中心对称色块（3x3十字、3x4胖十字、5x4胖菱形等），bbox至少3x3，左右+上下对称... → 箭头形精灵\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:10:# - The shared anchor color now forms several small arrow blobs instead of plus-like symmetric blobs.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:11:# - Each arrow is one of a few fixed templates, rotated to point U/D/L/R.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:12:# - Each arrow still owns exactly one colored seed tile and one grid keeps one ray pre-extended.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:14:#   (clockwise from the pointing direction), while the arrow's own facing direction tells us where the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:15:#   ray should go. Example: a right-pointing arrow has its seed directly below it, but the seed repeats\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:17:#   we must read the arrow shape and project \"right\".\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:19:# - If the seed stayed on the tip side, the task would visually collapse back toward the original.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:24:# - Each generated grid uses at least two arrow orientations so the orientation cue is actually visible.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:26:# - detect_dominant_big_component_color still works because arrows remain the only components with both\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:30:# - The original nozzle-span assert also depended on a plus arm/tip model and is no longer meaningful.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:35:#   wrong arrow and the solver sees exactly one adjacent non-arrow component per arrow.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:37:#   existing arrow-neighborhood guard cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:39:# - Human-solvable cue: arrows visibly point one way while their seed sits on a different side.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:40:# - The kept pre-extended ray demonstrates that the repeated pattern follows the arrow orientation, not\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:44:# - Rays do not overlap arrows and do not touch foreign arrows.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:51:# - For every generated arrow, the unique attachment side must be orthogonal to the ray direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:52:# - Per sample, at least two distinct arrow orientations should usually appear.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:54:# - Solver assumes every big anchor component exactly matches one rotated arrow template.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:55:# - Solver assumes each arrow has exactly one adjacent non-anchor component (seed or pre-extended ray).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:177:        \"launch\": (2, 2),  # canonical right-arrow: seed attaches below this cell\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:207:_CANONICAL_ATTACH_NORMAL = (1, 0)  # right-arrow seeds attach on the clockwise flank: below\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:255:def _oriented_arrow_spec(spec: dict, direction: str) -> tuple[np.ndarray, tuple[int, int], tuple[int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:262:def _match_arrow_direction(mask: np.ndarray) -> tuple[int, int] | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:299:    Extend marker tiles forward from arrow-shaped anchors by repeating them to the grid edge.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:303:    - A dominant non-bg color forms several small arrow sprites, possibly in different rotations.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:304:    - Each arrow has exactly one adjacent colored marker component; one of these rays may already be long.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:307:    - For each arrow, recognize which way the arrow points from its shape.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:309:    - Repeat that payload in the arrow's pointing direction until the boundary, without overwriting arrow pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:311:    Key insight: The marker's attachment side is no longer the direction cue; the arrow silhouette itself\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:319:    arrow_col = detect_do