ap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D15/2/code.py:29:#      the shared plus footprint, then use the tip color (8 here) to locate valid attachments.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D15/2/code.py:44:#      touch the arm-tip color specifically, so the solver now gathers candidate markers only from tip-colored\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D15/2/code.py:136:def detect_tip_color(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D15/2/code.py:145:    In this variant the marker is attached to the arm-tip color, so we use the repeated\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D15/2/code.py:249:    - Each plus-shaped anchor is now a shared two-color sprite: one interior color plus one arm-tip color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D15/2/code.py:250:    - Small colored seed tiles use other colors and touch the arm-tip color on exactly one side; one seed's ray is already pre-extended.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D15/2/code.py:254:    - Use the arm-tip color to find which marker component is attached to which side of each plus, then repeat that seed away from the plus until the boundary.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D15/2/code.py:274:    tip_color = detect_tip_color(g, plus_lab, int(pn), plus_pair)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D15/2/code.py:275:    if tip_color is None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D15/2/code.py:288:        tip_mask = plus_mask & (g == int(tip_color))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D15/2/code.py:290:        for r, c in np.argwhere(tip_mask):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D15/2/code.py:313:                    if 0 <= rr < H and 0 <= cc < W and bool(tip_mask[rr, cc]):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D15/2/code.py:387:    0 = empty, 1 = core color, 2 = arm-tip / boundary color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D15/2/code.py:525:    tip_color: int,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D15/2/code.py:564:                out[r, c] = int(core_color if role == 1 else tip_color)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D15/2/code.py:617:    core_color, tip_color = map(int, rng.choice(others, size=2, replace=False))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D15/2/code.py:618:    palette = [c for c in others if c not in {core_color, tip_color}]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D15/2/code.py:640:            tip_color,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7c66cb00/14/code.py:49:#     - output shows one chained trail of the same two-blob layout across multiple bars\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D1/1/code.py:42:#     - specific L-shaped local patterns were present at bbox corners\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f215267/D11/2/code.py:29:#     - Holes are repeated across multiple frames because total matching sprites is always >= 3.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7c66cb00/12/code.py:23:# - D9 changes the per-bar placement logic: once multiple patterns map to one bar, they\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7c66cb00/12/code.py:41:#   by at least one outer sprite and at least one bar receiving multiple patterns.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7c66cb00/12/code.py:286:    - The upper zone contains 6-8 detached sprites. Multiple sprites may share the same\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/3/code.py:99:#      changes multiple output cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D1/3/code.py:32:    - generator deliberately places geometrically TL/BR elbows using TR/BL-shaped Ls\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D18/0/code.py:22:#    - The original arm-tip / seed-span assertion depended on direction being tied to the touching arm. That is also\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D18/0/code.py:36:#    - Multiple directions are used within one grid whenever possible, giving the human solver repeated evidence that\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/23/code.py:104:- Objects are kept separated by background moats, so multiple colorful interiors do not merge.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/11/code.py:292:    - Away from the legend, every true marker color appears exactly once as two 3-pixel L corners that\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D1/2/code.py:28:#      5 pixels) while the other three are smaller Ls (arm length 2, 3 pixels).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D1/2/code.py:33:#      original: collect one color -> inspect which two corners contain 3-pixel L anchors -> fill the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D1/2/code.py:36:#      infer which diagonal that corner belongs to -> verify the opposite corner contains a 3-pixel L\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/10/code.py:32:#    - \"station size uniquely identifies the destination\" is false now; multiple real stations share\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/db0c5428/D9/2/code.py:17:# - Complexity calibration: the variant changes only multiplicity and placement.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/bf45cf4b/D3/1/code.py:26:#      The stamping loop is the same, but height and width multipliers diverge.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/bf45cf4b/D3/1/code.py:58:#      scaling visible across multiple copies.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/22/code.py:55:      mod_zero        -> exact multiple, grey remains but the object stays put\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/22/code.py:82:  - Regions are not overloaded with extra semantics like speed multipliers; this avoids\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/22/code.py:83:    a noisy interaction between multiple hidden rules and keeps the fusion readable.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/7/code.py:216:    assert len(pairs) <= 1, \"marker color has multiple valid same-shape diagonal pairs\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/7/code.py:248:    - Neither color alone nor shape frequency alone is sufficient here. Color narrows the search, shape identifies which\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D1/4/code.py:146:    - Outside the legend, each active marker color appears as two mirrored 3-pixel L corners.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/6/code.py:26:#     The final box is two cells narrower and the surviving interior contains two bg holes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/17/code.py:42:#      2-5 legend entries, optional noop rows, both diagonals, and multiple bbox\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/17/code.py:48:#      L-pairs whenever possible so the solver is clearly handling multiple\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/17/code.py:466:    \"\"\"Choose legend entry types while preserving multiple real L-pairs.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7c66cb00/D2/1/code.py:42:#    sprites so multiple examples support the rule.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7c66cb00/D2/1/code.py:68:#    notice those narrow edge pixels. We also force at least one two-tone\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/18/code.py:308:      that color; a bg cell visited by multiple different ray colors becomes the special marker 9.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a251c730/D5/1/code.py:56:#     - because crop size now varies with marker positions, multiple samples visibly differ in shape.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D16/1/code.py:18:#     - A legend marker color may appear once in multiple bands. Those repeated same-color objects are the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D16/1/code.py:48:#     - At least one legend marker is reused in multiple bands in every generated puzzle, so the variant\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D16/1/code.py:271:MULTI_BAND_REUSE_PROB = 0.75    # non-forced entries often appear in multiple bands too\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/4/code.py:782:def _place_docked_trains(base, bg, regions, label_pool, arrow_color, n_trains, shared_size=None):\n/hom