arker component, and the seed bbox matches the relevant arm-tip\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D10/0/code.py:214:    - Read the arm-tip span from that component's own outer edge, require the seed bbox to match that local nozzle width, and then repeat the seed tile away from the '+'.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D3/1/code.py:111:    - Away from the legend, each active marker color appears either as two L-shaped corner markers on one bbox diagonal or as a solid 2x2 block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/db0c5428/D1/1/code.py:55:#     minor colors only provide asymmetric detail. No hidden ordering by color id\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/2/code.py:29:#    - `_l_anchor_present` still assumes each marker corner is a 3-pixel L; unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/2/code.py:168:    - Away from the legend, each active marker color appears either as two opposite 3-pixel L corners or as a solid 2x2 block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D3/3/code.py:178:    - Outside the legend, each active marker color appears either as two diagonal L-shaped corners\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/bf45cf4b/18/code.py:24:- This combo changes both source-object multiplicity and source-target cardinality:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/bf45cf4b/18/code.py:43:- Picking one non-tile component as the control is invalid: there are multiple controls.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/bf45cf4b/18/code.py:53:- Control sprites are first laid out on an abstract group canvas with 1-3 pixel gaps, ensuring\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/bf45cf4b/18/code.py:59:- Humans can see one decorative square tile and multiple differently colored mask-like controls.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/bf45cf4b/18/code.py:78:- `main()` assumes each control expands independently and the final output contains multiple\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D11/0/code.py:26:# - Input therefore contains one plus with multiple visible seeds around it; exactly one\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D11/0/code.py:50:# - `adj_ids` may contain multiple components for one plus; this was already supported by the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D11/0/code.py:55:# - The nozzle-span alignment checks assume the seed tile is flush with the arm tip. Generator\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D11/0/code.py:200:    own multiple independent seeds, and each seed defines its own ray by attachment side.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/bf45cf4b/D13/0/code.py:30:#      multiple times. The generator guarantees a symmetric tile with all four\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D3/2/code.py:199:    - Away from the legend, a marker color appears either as two opposite L-shaped corners of one bounding box or as a solid 2x2 block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/9/code.py:35:# - At least one legend entry is reused across multiple bands, ensuring the partitioned processing is visible and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/9/code.py:60:# - The three fused signals are all directly visible: multiple background bands, an off-corner edge legend, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/9/code.py:71:#   same actual marker color in multiple bands.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/1/code.py:14:     * D2: a 3-pixel outer segment emits from all 3 segment pixels, not only its two ends;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/1/code.py:31:   - To keep the combo legible, the generator only allows full 3-pixel segments.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/1/code.py:57:   - For each chosen edge, the generator builds the 3-pixel segment, then computes three full\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/1/code.py:180:    - Each outer segment is a straight 3-pixel diagonal component in its own color, separate from the diamond color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/14/code.py:38:#    - Original / D14 code assumed either multiple markers or a unique orthogonal mate could be\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7c66cb00/D3/4/code.py:74:#   - proximity grouping is supported by repeated examples because multiple top objects use the same rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D7/0/code.py:29:#    - The alignment asserts still depend on each seed bbox matching the arm-tip span exactly.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D7/0/code.py:227:            # Alignment check: seed cross-axis span must match arm tip span.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/10/code.py:79:     same legend row applies to multiple repeated strips of one marker color, the direction code gets\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/10/code.py:381:    - The L shapes no longer tell you the diagonal to fill. They only provide coordinates for axis-aligned pairing; the diagonal choice is encoded visibly in the legend's left-versus-right color order and reused across several same-colored pairs.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/10/code.py:431:# ── CFG: per-entry multiplicity ────────────────────────────────────\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D17/0/code.py:47:#    - Generated examples are rejected unless top-down and bottom-up execution differ by multiple cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a251c730/D1/1/code.py:32:#     - Because each sample contains two types with repeated markers or repeated source copies, the \"majority color is the key\" rule is supported multiple times within one grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/3/code.py:202:    The visible point is already the chosen emitting endpoint, not the midpoint of a hidden 3-pixel segment,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/db0c5428/D12/2/code.py:72:#     - When there are multiple wrong cells, generation forces a mix of background and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/bf45cf4b/D6/2/code.py:48:#    - T