/5/code.py:60:    - Thin bands create much less clutter than full-triangle fills, which helps when multiple entries coexist.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7c66cb00/D4/1/code.py:62:  Widths stay in a narrow range and fills remain unique, preventing ambiguity.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D4/1/code.py:144:    - Elsewhere, each marker color appears either as two opposite L-shaped bbox corners or as a solid 2x2 block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/26/code.py:42:#     can see the same source color propagated into multiple destinations.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/26/code.py:225:        assert sid not in used, \"destination sprites should not receive multiple leaves\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D2/3/code.py:69:#     - Each cavity uses only two colors, repeated across multiple cells by the checkerboard,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/2/code.py:12:#    - Small trace: suppose a TR outer segment is the 3-pixel diagonal\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/2/code.py:26:#      boundary. A 2-pixel segment is a contiguous subsegment of the canonical 3-pixel outer\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/2/code.py:29:#      (4-step vs 6-step bundles) and at least one 3-pixel segment where D2 is visibly\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/2/code.py:55:#    - A human sees two repeated regularities: 3-pixel segments produce denser 3-lane bundles\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D5/1/code.py:14:#    - Example: if the left chain uses colors [2, 4, 6] from root to tail and the right chain\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D5/1/code.py:723:                is_tail = piece_idx == chain_len - 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D5/1/code.py:724:                if is_tail:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D5/1/code.py:739:                if is_tail:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7c66cb00/D4/2/code.py:70:#       borders, and occupy multiple row bands.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/13/code.py:41:#       ambiguous because a full rectangle can accidentally satisfy multiple L-corner tests. The generator therefore\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/bf45cf4b/D11/0/code.py:75:# - Multiple colors are preserved exactly; there is no hidden recoloring map to guess.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/bf45cf4b/D11/0/code.py:107:    - Its bbox patch `sprite` may contain multiple colors and background holes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/31/code.py:218:    assert len(sprites) >= 3, \"expected multiple bordered sprites\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/bf45cf4b/15/code.py:55:# - The rule space is intentionally narrow: exactly one component, one mask, and exactly 2 rounds.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/bf45cf4b/15/code.py:122:    - Its cropped patch `sprite` may contain multiple colors and background holes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/16/code.py:15:#       same_geometry: 3-pixel diagonal segment (or 2 if clipped) one step outside a diamond edge\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a251c730/D12/1/code.py:15:#   - The rule is unchanged, but the same color can now play multiple roles at once, so the grid is visually more ambiguous.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/db0c5428/D6/1/code.py:53:#   multiple of 3; the generator preserves that exactly.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/23/code.py:49:#    - Distractors are removed, but multiple legend entries remain and their bboxes are packed\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4a21e3da/D9/0/code.py:42:#     - the variant is only visible if split pixels are numerous enough and touch multiple regions, so the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D5/2/code.py:18:#   depth 1 is recolored to the \"next\" legend color, and a depth-2 tail is recolored to the second-next\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D5/2/code.py:770:                is_tail = piece_idx == chain_len - 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D5/2/code.py:771:                if is_tail:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D5/2/code.py:786:                if is_tail:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D13/1/code.py:41:      to be genuine L-pairs whose fill masks overlap on multiple background cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D13/1/code.py:306:    - Outside the legend, each marker color appears either as two L-shaped opposite corners of a bbox or as a solid 2x2 block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/27/code.py:163:      - border color appears multiple times\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D1/0/code.py:26:#    - Fill colors are intentionally reused across multiple cavities, so solving cannot collapse\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/9/code.py:16:#     old: 2-3 pixel diagonal segment, one per chosen diamond edge\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/9/code.py:17:#     new: 3-pixel L marker occupying three cells of a 2x2 block\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/9/code.py:22:#     new: infer outward diagonal directly from the L bend orientation; the two degree-1 tips\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/9/code.py:23:#          emit rays, and the ray direction is the sum of the two unit arm vectors from bend to tips\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/9/code.py:31:#     从 bend 到两个 tips 的单位向量分别是 (-1,0) 和 (0,+1)，其和为 (-1,+1)，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/9/code.py:40:#     - 原 _outer_line_info 假设外部组件共线；L 标记下完全失效，必须用 4 邻域度数找 bend/tips。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/9/code.py:58:#     这样输入里每个局部结构都很清楚：一个 5x5 方框，周围若干小 L，输出再从对应 tips 拉出对角线。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/9/code.py:63:#     - marker 必须是 3 像素、4 邻域下唯一 bend + 两个 tips 的 L；生成器只放这种模板。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/9/code.py:65:#     - 射线方向必须是 tips 相对 bend 的两个单位向量之和；模板构造保证恰好得到四个非轴向对角方向。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/9/code.py:136:    tips = [p for p, d in deg.items() if d == 1]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/9/code.py:137:    if len(bends) != 1 or len(tips) != 2:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/9/code.py:141:    arm_vecs = [(tr - bend[0], tc - bend[1]) for tr, tc in tips]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/9/code.py:153:        \"tips\": sorted(tips),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/9/code.py:169:    Extend diagonal rays from L-shaped corner markers around hollow square rings on a checkerboard.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/9/code.py:177:    - For each L marker, find the unique bend cell of 4-neighbor degree 2 and the two degree-1 tips.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/9/code.py:178:    - The diagonal ray direction is the sum of the two unit vectors from the bend to those tips.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/9/code.py:179:      Starting from each tip, paint background cells in that direction with the marker color until\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/9/code.py:223:            for pr, pc in minfo[\"tips\"]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/9/code.py:301:        tips = list(info[\"tips\"])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/9/code.py:303:        rays = _ray_cells((h, w), tips[0], outward) + _ray_cells((h, w), tips[1], outward)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/8/code.py:14:      - replace the single global grey trail with multiple disconnected grey components\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/8/code.py:115:      - border color appears multiple times\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/8/code.py:240:    - Grey cells form multiple disconnected thin path components, and each component touches an ordered chain of\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/8/code.py:263:    assert len(grey_comps) >= 2, \"expected multiple grey components\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/6/code.py:44:#    objects inside a narrow interior activity strip aligned with the long grid\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/6/code.py:46:#    input, and preserves multiple repeated examples of the same rule.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/6/code.py:68:#    Active objects share one narrow strip but do not overlap after expansion.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/6/code.py:348:    \"\"\"Pick a long-thin bbox sized to fit multiple visible objects in one strip.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D18/1/code.py:293:    - Most legend markers appear as two opposite L-shaped corners plus one separate same-color direction pixel on the bbox edge.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D1/1/code.py:248:            raise ValueError(\"shape multiplicity mismatch\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/10/code.py:16:#    - Original task: a hollow diamond has a short 3-pixel diagonal segment outside each chosen edge;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/10/code.py:19:#      become the arm tips N/S/W/E, and the natural rays become cardinal instead of diagonal.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/10/code.py:20:#    - D6 then compresses each 3-pixel outer segment into its center pixel only.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/10/code.py:21:#    - Fused result: each chosen arm keeps only one point marker one step beyond the arm tip:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/10/code.py:23:#      The point is interpreted as the midpoint of the hidden 3-pixel segment that would have appeared\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/10/code.py:26:#    - Difference from source: shape reasoning switches from diamond edges to plus arm tips, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/10/code.py:140:    - Zero or more single-pixel markers, each sitting just beyond one arm tip of a plus.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/10/code.py:143:    - Treat each marker as the midpoint of a hidden 3-pixel segment orthogonal to that arm's ray direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a251c730/D4/0/code.py:54:#      appear in multiple orientations across one example.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7c66cb00/D14/0/code.py:55:#       holds once multiple patterns can want the same bar interval. It is replaced by\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D1/3/code.py:52:#    same limited 3-7 fill colors are reused across multiple cavities, so humans infer\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/14/code.py:32:#      (`arm=2`, 3 pixels) and exactly one is larger. The large arm length is either 3, 4, or 5.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/14/code.py:84:#      rather than multiple `(marker, fill)` rows.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/14/code.py:345:            tail = solve(used | mask)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/14/code.py:346:            if tail is not None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/14/code.py:347:                memo[used] = [mask] + tail\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/21/code.py:12:#   - D6 changes the outer object from a collinear segment into a 3-pixel L marker. Direction is no\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/21/code.py:13:#     longer read from line slope; instead the marker bend and two tips determine a diagonal outward\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/21/code.py:15:#     bend (r0-1,c0+4), tips above/right of the bend, and therefore outward direction (-1,+1).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/21/code.py:21:#       * output: the TR marker grows two NE rays from its tips, while the BR marker stays unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/21/code.py:52:#     short outer glyphs are L-shaped instead of straight, and only the upward-facing Ls elongate.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/21/code.py:141:    tips = [p for p, d in deg.items() if d == 1]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/21/code.py:142:    if len(bends) != 1 or len(tips) != 2:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/21/code.py:146:    arm_vecs = [(tr - bend[0], tc - bend[1]) for tr, tc in tips]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/21/code.py:156:    return {\"bend\": bend, \"tips\": sorted(tips), \"outward\": outward}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/21/code.py:180:    - Short 3-pixel L markers near square corners in other non-background colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/21/code.py:183:    - Recognize each L marker by its bend and two arm tips, then infer its diagonal outward direction\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/21/code.py:184:      as the sum of the two unit bend-to-tip vectors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/21/code.py:186:      direction emit rays. From each active tip, cast a diagonal ray in the marker color until a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/21/code.py:190:    - Direction no longer comes from a line segment slope. The L shape itself encodes the ray\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/21/code.py:232:            for sr, sc in info[\"tips\"]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/21/code.py:335:            rays = _ray_cells((h, w), info[\"tips\"][0], info[\"outward\"]) + _ray_cells(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/21/code.py:336:                (h, w), info[\"tips\"][-1], info[\"outward\"]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/33/code.py:36:#    The cascade is intentionally narrow: one ordered chain, one visible comparison key per step, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/33/code.py:139:      - border color appears multiple times\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D2/1/code.py:693:          