mbo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:3:# Name: 带对角标记的精灵+方向箭头标记\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:15:#   a 2-pixel arrow stub made from the transferable payload color,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:19:#   source.arrow -> dominant-axis direction to the target destination,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:32:#   in the encoded arrow direction. So arrow direction alone is insufficient.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:34:#   corners compatible with the chosen arrow direction. This keeps the symbolic alphabet small.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:42:#   that border class and then resolve the target by arrow direction plus marker quadrant.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:43:# - The D15-style directional cue is compressed to a 2-pixel center+neighbor arrow stub. That\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:46:#   3-pixel arrow while remaining a single readable object.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:51:# - Sources are always fully visible 3x3 boxes so both the arrow and the diagonal marker are\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:53:# - Source placement is filtered so the two destinations are both in the source's arrow direction\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:58:# - The input visibly contains two deleted source boxes, each with an arrow and an extra corner\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:65:# - The arrow is a compact 2-pixel center+edge pointer, while the marker remains a single corner\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:74:# - Real sources are full 3x3 boxes with color multiplicities exactly {6,2,1}: guaranteed.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:75:# - For each real source, both destinations share the arrow direction but occupy the two marker\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:152:    assert patch[mr, mc] == border_color, \"marker corner must not overlap the arrow\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:372:      - border color appears multiple times\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:409:def _detect_arrow_marker_sources(g: np.ndarray, bg: int, grey: int) -> list[dict]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:412:    The payload forms one of four 2-pixel arrow stubs and includes the center cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:413:    The marker is a singleton corner not occupied by the arrow.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:523:    - Each real source box has three simultaneous parts: a shared border color, a 2-pixel payload-colored arrow stub, and one extra diagonal marker pixel in a corner.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:529:    - Among those same-border candidates, keep the unique source whose arrow points toward the destination and whose diagonal marker corner matches the destination's quadrant relative to that source.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:533:    - Matching is now layered: the destination center color selects a source border class, the arrow gives a coarse global direction, and the diagonal marker resolves which destination inside that direction cone is the true target.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:540:    sources = _detect_arrow_marker_sources(g, bg, grey)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:542:    assert sources, \"expected marked arrow sources\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/17/code.py:770:    sources = _detect_arrow_marker_sources(g, bg, GREY)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/23/code.py:232:#   clipped 2-3 pixel diagonal and every diamond must remain a valid 5x5 hollow out